# Follow atf-guide for ATF Implementation

When implementing or modifying ServiceNow Automated Test Framework (ATF) tests, always follow `atf-guide` via Now SDK. Do not guess ATF steps, methods, or category namespaces.

## How to Read Guide

Before implementing or editing any ATF test:

```bash
# Preview topic structure
npx @servicenow/sdk explain atf-guide --peek --format=raw

# Read full ATF implementation guide
npx @servicenow/sdk explain atf-guide --format=raw
```

## Mandatory Rules

- **Consult `atf-guide` first**: Run `npx @servicenow/sdk explain atf-guide --format=raw` for API signatures across all 13 ATF categories (`atf.server`, `atf.form`, `atf.rest`, `atf.uiTestScript`, `atf.applicationNavigator`, `atf.list`, `atf.form_SP`, `atf.catalog`, `atf.catalog_SP`, `atf.email`, `atf.reporting`, `atf.responsiveDashboard`).
- **Follow Fluent ATF test structure**:
  ```typescript
  import { Test } from "@servicenow/sdk/core";
  import "@servicenow/sdk/global";

  Test({
    $id: Now.ID["test_id"],
    name: "test name",
    description: "meaningful description",
    failOnServerError: true,
  }, (atf) => {
    // Sequential steps using atf.<category>.<method>
  });
  ```
- **Reconcile test suite on logic change**:
  - **Added logic**: Add corresponding positive and negative ATF tests.
  - **Changed logic**: Update existing test assertions to match the new behavior.
  - **Removed logic**: Delete obsolete tests asserting removed logic.
- **Related guides**: For custom UI (SPAs, UI Pages), check `npx @servicenow/sdk explain atf-ui-test-script-guide --format=raw`.
